  "summary": "The first time that Peter laid eyes on Tony Stark in the flesh, he'd been more than a little starstruck. This was the man who was everything he wanted to be. A superhero who was saving the world every few days. He could build anything at all and had all the resources in the world to do it. The idea that Mr. Stark wanted him, who just patrolled through Queens a couple times a week, made his brain a little dizzy. In that moment, he would've given Mr. Stark anything he'd asked for.\nIf Mr. Stark had asked, he'd have given up his identity at the time, probably.\nMaybe it should've been the first red flag that Tony had let him keep it secret, considering he was preaching to Captain America about transparency and accountability.",
